        setup: {
          players: 'Minimum Players: 2\nMaximum Players: 6\nOptimal Players: 2 or 4 (partnerships)\nPartnerships: Optional for 4 or 6 players',
          deck: 'Type: 40-card Italian or stripped 52-card deck (no 8s, 9s, 10s). Suits: coins, cups, swords, batons (Latin) or diamonds, hearts, clubs, spades (French). Ranks: King=10, Horse/Queen=9, Jack=8, 7–2 face value, Ace=1.\nNumber of Decks: 1\nJokers: Not included',
          equipment: '40-card deck\nScore sheet (optional)\nTable space',
          dealing: 'Three cards to each player, then four cards face up to the table; deal one at a time. After each round of three plays, deal three more to each player (no new table cards). Direction: counter-clockwise with 3+ players.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Capture cards from the table by matching rank or by matching the sum of two or more table cards; score points for sweeps (scopa), most cards, most coins/diamonds, the seven of coins (settebello), and the best primiera; first to 11 or more points wins the game.',
          gameplay: '1. Deal: Each player receives three cards; four cards are dealt face up to the table; remaining cards form the stock.\n2. Play: Non-dealer plays first. On each turn, play one card from hand. If it matches a single table card by value, capture that card; if it equals the sum of two or more table cards, capture that set; otherwise leave the played card on the table. When you capture all table cards (sweep), that is a scopa and scores 1 point.\n3. After each player has played three cards, the dealer gives three more cards to each player (no new table cards). Repeat until all cards are played.\n4. End of hand: Remaining table cards go to the last captor. Score for scope, most cards, most coins, settebello, and best primiera. First to 11+ points wins.',
          keyRules: [
            "Capture by matching one table card's value or the sum of multiple table cards; if both options exist, you must take the single card.",
            'Capturing is compulsory when possible; you may choose to play a card that does not capture only when it cannot capture.',
            "Sweeping all table cards (scopa) scores 1 point; dealer's last card of the hand never counts as a scopa.",
            'At end of hand, score 1 point each for: most cards, most coins/diamonds, having the seven of coins, and best primiera (one card per suit using Seven=21, Six=18, Ace=16, etc.).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Capture when you can; prefer taking coins/diamonds and high primiera cards (sevens, sixes, aces). Avoid leaving table cards that let the next player make a scopa.',
          intermediate: 'Track which coins and high cards have been played; delay or force sweeps to deny the opponent scope; when choosing between captures, take the set that improves your primiera or coin count.',
          advanced: 'Set up sweeps for yourself by leaving sums that only your hand can make; block opponent sweeps by taking key cards or playing a card that forces a non-sweep capture; in primiera, prioritise capturing aces and sixes.',
          tips: [
            'The seven of coins (settebello) is worth one point and is key for primiera; try to capture it.',
            'If you can capture with a single card or a set, you must take the single card; use this rule when it helps you.',
            "Leaving the table empty after your capture (scopa) scores a point and can disrupt the opponent's plans.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
